    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Corbin Carroll** stands out as the clear anchor of the lineup with an elite 85.94 score. His matchup against Mikolas is ideal, and with a slow delivery from the opposing starter creating a +4% boost to his already high stolen base equity, **Corbin Carroll** is our primary source of speed-category production. **Gabriel Moreno** and **Austin Riley** also grade out as high-tier starts above 70.0. **Austin Riley** benefits immensely from a park factor boost (+16%), while **Gabriel Moreno** continues to capitalize on the favorable matchup against Mikolas (4.71 xERA) and an elevated spot in the order. Meanwhile, **Isaac Paredes** continues to prove his worth in the 3-hole, as his platoon advantage and strong SP skill modifier against Fedde make him a mandatory start for power stability.\n\nWe are forced to navigate a difficult matchup for **Josh Naylor**, whose score sits at a marginal 49.47 due to the daunting presence of deGrom on the mound. While he stays in the lineup to avoid wasted starts, his production ceiling is severely capped by the elite SP skill adjustment. The most difficult bench decision involved **Travis Bazzana** (39.05), who failed to clear our 40-point \"Zebras Floor\" threshold by less than a point. While **Travis Bazzana** showed potential in his underlying metrics, the combination of a sub-optimal park factor and negative SP skill adjustment against Rasmussen ultimately kept him on the bench in favor of more efficient platoon fits like **Mickey Moniak**, who provides a necessary dynamic platoon boost (+14%) despite facing a tough arm in Misiorowski.\n\nRisks remain throughout the afternoon, specifically regarding the \"Lineup Pending\" status for **Jose Caballero**. While our projected model accounts for an 8th-order slot, any drop lower in the lineup would further cannibalize his already marginal 51.08 score, particularly given the 2.82 xERA of S\u00e1nchez. We are also monitoring the remaining bench assets; with **Giancarlo Stanton** and **Trevor Story** still lingering on the IL, our depth is thin. Should **Vinnie Pasquantino**, **Max Muncy**, **Zach McKinstry**, **Dalton Rushing**, **Edwin Arroyo**, or **Henry Bolte** see a significant change in their projected platoon windows, we are prepared to adjust our approach for tomorrow, but for now, we are prioritizing the high-upside speed profiles of **Corbin Carroll** and **James Wood** to secure our standing in the standings.",
